This is a Bash script designed to migrate specific local repository configurations from a Source JFrog Platform Deployment (JPD) to a Target JPD.

This script automates the process of checking for the existence of specific local repositories on a Target JFrog Platform Deployment (JPD) and, if they do not exist, Creates the repository with same configuration as in Source JPD  to the Target JPD using the JFrog CLI.

It ensures that only the repository configuration (.json file) is migrated, not the artifacts within.

Prerequisites
Before running this script, ensure the following tools and files are available:

Bash Shell: The script must be executed in a Bash environment (Linux/macOS or WSL on Windows).

JFrog CLI (jf): Must be installed and configured on your system.

jq: The lightweight and flexible command-line JSON processor is required for parsing API responses.

JFrog Platform Deployments (JPDs): Both Source and Target JPDs must be accessible.

Configured Server IDs: You must have configured the connection details for your Source and Target JPDs using jf c add (e.g., jf c add source-jpd --url=<URL> --access-token=<Token>).

cachelocals.txt file: This file must exist in the same directory as the script and contain a list of local repository keys (names), one per line, that you intend to migrate.

Execution:

Syntax:
./migrate_repos.sh <SOURCE_SERVER_ID> <TARGET_SERVER_ID>

Example:
./migrate_repos.sh source-server target-server
